        "problem": "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=\u27e8$  \n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\u27e9$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(0)+(-2)(5)+(1)(-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{0-10-1}{9+4+1}\\,\u27e83,-2,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{14}\\,\u27e83,-2,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-\\frac{33}{14},\\frac{11}{7},-\\frac{11}{14}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n`",
